   - Plan and implement the first slice of M2 delete logic: `rb_delete`'s top-level BST-splice orchestration only, explicitly deferring all `delete_fixup` rebalancing logic to a future slice. This required plan-mode approval per CLAUDE.md's rule that algorithmic changes (especially delete fixup) need a pre-approved plan enumerating every fixup case and memory-free path.
   - Before accepting the code, the user twice rejected in-flight Edit tool calls to demand plain-language explanations first: (a) what a "sentinel node" NIL representation would mean/cost vs. the plan's chosen explicit `x_parent` parameter approach, and (b) whether `rb_delete` rotates and why multiple `transplant` calls exist. Only after these explanations did the user approve applying the edit.
   - Requested PROMPTLOG.md entries be "focused on my prompting and questioning" rather than deep technical/logical detail; ultimately told the assistant to drop the sentinel-node PROMPTLOG entry entirely and return to implementation.
